// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'EnumerationMapping'. Valid alternatives: [',']
//
// A transformer is a PREFIX on the mapped operation:
//     kind: EnumerationMapping KindMapping: [db]T.KIND
// with its own trailing colon. It is not a suffix on the column, and it is not an optional
// tail of the property mapping.
//
// Written the other way round it reads like the natural thing -- name the column, then say
// how to transform it -- and a rewrite that parses the right-hand side as an operation
// followed by optional annotations accepts it. The same position is shared with the Binding
// transformer, so getting it wrong moves both.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::EnumTransformerPostfix
(
   fixture::neg::Person: Relational
   {
      ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db]T
      kind: [fixture::neg::Db]T.KIND EnumerationMapping KindMapping
   }
)
